  "lineage": "Song tradition of the Arab-descended, largely Hadhrami communities of Indonesia and the Malay peninsula, named for the gambus, a short-necked lute of the oud family (the oud card stands in). Orkes gambus bands set Arabic and Malay lyrics for voice with gambus, violin and small marwas hand drums (the generic hand-drum card stands in), and play for weddings, community celebrations and the zapin dance; mid-twentieth-century bands recorded widely.",
